    <string name="how_title">HOW TO PLAY</string>
    <string name="how_intro">Every card shows one number. Decide whether it is prime, composite, or neither.</string>
    <string name="how_prime_title">PRIME NUMBERS</string>
    <string name="how_prime_body">A prime is a whole number greater than 1 with exactly two positive divisors: 1 and itself.</string>
    <string name="how_prime_examples">Examples: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11</string>
    <string name="how_composite_title">COMPOSITE NUMBERS</string>
    <string name="how_composite_body">A composite is a whole number greater than 1 with more than two positive divisors.</string>
    <string name="how_composite_examples">Examples: 4, 6, 8, 9, 10</string>
    <string name="how_neither_title">NEITHER PRIME NOR COMPOSITE</string>
    <string name="how_neither_body">The number 1 has only one positive divisor, itself. It is neither prime nor composite.</string>
    <string name="how_play_title">HOW A ROUND WORKS</string>
    <string name="how_play_body">In Classic, swipe right for prime and left for not prime. A correct answer adds a point; a wrong answer or a timeout ends the run.</string>
